  "openQuestions": [
    "Webflow component shape: the five forms have different fields, so a single component with text props cannot hold them. Proposal: one Webflow component with slots for the form, details and links, and component variants for script heading (h1 style + text-style-script + is-rotated) versus caps heading (heading-style-h2, contact page). If slots are not wanted, reuse the class family without a component and make only the identical legal/corporate pair a component.",
    "contact/01-contact-us: what fills the grey #D9D9D9 placeholder (905x726)? A map embed, an image, or something else. The plan keeps an empty figure with the placeholder colour.",
    "contact/01-contact-us: instagram and facebook URLs are not in the design.",
    "Form handling: where should the five forms submit (Webflow form notifications to which address, or an external endpoint)? Field names in instances are proposals.",
    "Date and time fields: native type=date and type=time inputs replace the placeholder with the browser picker, which breaks the design. The plan uses type=text; confirm, or accept native pickers.",
    "Container width: the Figma frame is 1600 wide with content about 1482 wide (about 59px gutters), wider than container-large (80rem). The plan uses container-large, so at 1440 the content is 1280 wide. K01 may want one site-wide wider container.",
    "is-clipped button: Webflow's style panel may not expose clip-path. If it does not, the Designer session adds the clip-path rule through a site-wide custom CSS embed, or uses the vector-25 SVG as a stretched background image."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Colour #2B2927 (form labels, fieldset headings) has no variable; the plan uses color-neutral-900 (#262118), the nearest token. Visual difference is negligible.",
    "contact/01-contact-us labels use EYEBROW-CAPS (18px) in Figma; the plan uses text-style-caps-caption-16 (16px) for every detail label so the class family stays one set. Its heading uses heading-style-h2 in color-neutral-900 rather than color-accent (#29310C).",
    "legal and corporate specs include an 'A Landmark Reimagined' heading (Sackers 40, cream) above the section bounds; it sits on the dark background of the previous band and is not part of this component. The brief's 'sackers-40' heading size therefore is not used.",
    "contact/01-contact-us spec includes the guild-nav-full-dark nav instance; the nav is a separate global component and is excluded.",
    "Field labels are rendered as styled placeholders with aria-label as the accessible name, matching the design (label sits on the underline), instead of visible label elements.",
    "Instance vertical spacing in the base crops varies (top 94px to 219px); the plan uses padding-section-large for every base instance.",
    "Field underlines in Figma are #262118 rectangles but render as a light hairline in the crops; the plan uses rgba(38, 33, 24, 0.35) (color-neutral-900 at 35%). No variable exists for it; the Designer may use the neutral-900 variable with alpha if available.",
    "The submit button and caps labels render narrower in the preview than Figma (button about 197px vs 234px) because Copperplate stands in for Sackers Heavy Gothic; padding follows the Figma vector exactly, so recheck on the live site with the real font before changing it."
  ],
  "k01": {
    "reconciledBy": "K01, 2026-10-20",
    "sharedClasses": "docs/figma/build-plans/shared-classes.md",
    "changes": [
      "Class list `heading-style-h1 text-style-script` is now `text-style-script`.",
      "Class list `form-split-script-contact_detail-label text-size-regular text-style-caps-caption-16` is now `form-split-script-contact_detail-label text-style-caps-caption-16`.",
      "Class list `form-split-script-contact_link text-size-regular text-style-caps-caption-16` is now `form-split-script-contact_link text-style-caps-caption-16`.",
      "Class list `button is-clipped` is now `button is-chamfer is-dark`.",
      "Submit button is `button is-chamfer is-dark` (was `is-clipped`); type is Label/Button instead of CAPS-CAPTION-16.",
      "Script heading uses the live `text-style-script` (Morello 60/72); its tablet and mobile steps are a live correction.",
      "Variables use live CSS names (`--_primitives---colors--*`, `--_typography---font-styles--*`)."
    ]
